# Anchorhead, the Illustrated Edition, played through all five days to the
# end. The route is the classic one: the keys from the real estate office,
# the house from attic to crypt, the courthouse records and the library,
# the old man on the vacant lot, the safe, the telescope, the well behind
# the slaughterhouse, the church and the sewers, the temple under the
# house, the mill, the asylum, the train, and the lighthouse.
#
# Where the game pauses for a key press, a line of "z" stands for the key,
# since any line is taken as one. Where the play turns on chance, a SEED
# directive pins it: the way out of the labyrinth of streets, where the
# buoy lies in the fog, and how fast the madman closes in.
